2026-05-01T10:56:52.766Z JOY-013D-5B item.created "Make ai init auto-accept detected doc paths" [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-01T10:56:58.154Z JOY-013D-5B comment.added "Plan:\n\n1. In `resolve_doc_path` (crates/joy-cli/src/commands/ai.rs:568): when `configured.is_none()` and `suggested_doc_path` returns an existing candidate, take it silently without prompting and persist it in project.yaml (only if it differs from the built-in default).\n\n2. In `check_docs` output (ai.rs:507-509): annotate freshly auto-detected paths so the user can see they were just picked up, e.g. `✔ CONTRIBUTING.md (auto-detected)`.\n\n3. After the loop, if any path was newly persisted, print a one-line hint: change paths with `joy project set docs.<key> <path>`.\n\n4. In the `configured but missing on disk` branch (ai.rs:510): before offering to create a template at the configured path, run `suggested_doc_path` again. If an existing candidate is found, prompt to switch to it (Y/n) and update project.yaml. Only fall back to the existing template-creation flow when nothing is found.\n\n5. Net effect: prompts only appear when there is a real decision to make (nothing detected anywhere). Detection events are surfaced in the output instead of swallowed." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
