2026-05-01T11:48:40.777Z JOY-013E-BC item.created "Make ai init gitignore block additive only" [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-01T11:48:53.842Z JOY-013E-BC comment.added "Plan:\n\n1. Add helper `existing_managed_block_entries(root) -> Vec<String>` in `crates/joy-cli/src/commands/ai.rs`. It reads `.gitignore`, locates the `### joy:start ... ### joy:end` markers and returns the non-empty trimmed lines between them. Returns empty vec if the file or block is missing.\n\n2. Change `update_gitignore` in `ai.rs` to be additive:\n   - Build the base entries from `GITIGNORE_BASE_ENTRIES` plus entries for tools in `configured_tools` (as today).\n   - Read the existing block. For each tool in `TOOL_GITIGNORE_ENTRIES` not already added (i.e. not currently configured), include its entries if at least one of them appears in the existing block.\n   - Iteration order stays fixed (the TOOL_GITIGNORE_ENTRIES order), so the resulting block is deterministic.\n\n3. The reset path (`joy ai reset` with no remaining tools, ai.rs:854) keeps the existing replace semantics so the user can still reset cleanly. The single-tool reset path already does not touch the gitignore.\n\n4. New unit tests:\n   - `update_gitignore_preserves_other_tools_block_entries`: existing block has all four tools, init runs with claude only -> block keeps all four.\n   - `update_gitignore_adds_newly_configured_tool`: existing block has claude only, init runs with claude+qwen -> block has both.\n   - `update_gitignore_does_not_resurrect_unrelated_lines`: only well-known tool entries are preserved; foreign lines inside the block are not.\n\n5. Net effect: drift between machines disappears; mixed setups are unaffected (Joy still only manages entries for tools it knows, and never invents new ones)." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-01T11:48:56.735Z JOY-013E-BC item.status_changed "new -> in-progress" [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-01T11:52:16.735Z JOY-013E-BC comment.added "Implemented in commit 5b4eb10.\n\nChanges in `crates/joy-cli/src/commands/ai.rs`:\n\n- [x] Added helper `existing_managed_block_entries(root)` that reads `.gitignore`, locates the joy:start/joy:end markers and returns the trimmed non-empty lines inside the block.\n- [x] Reworked `update_gitignore` to be additive: it now iterates `TOOL_GITIGNORE_ENTRIES` and includes a tool's entries when either (a) the tool is currently configured locally, or (b) at least one of its entries is already present in the existing block. Iteration order is fixed, so the resulting block stays deterministic.\n- [x] Reset path (`joy ai reset` with no remaining tools, ai.rs:854) is unchanged -- a full reset still resets the block to base entries.\n- [x] Added unit tests:\n    - `update_gitignore_preserves_other_tools_block_entries`\n    - `update_gitignore_adds_newly_configured_tool`\n    - `update_gitignore_does_not_resurrect_unrelated_lines`\n    - `update_gitignore_creates_block_from_scratch_when_absent`\n    - `existing_managed_block_entries_returns_empty_when_no_block`\n    - `existing_managed_block_entries_returns_empty_when_no_gitignore`\n\nVerification: `cargo test -p joy-cli` (ai module 23 passed), `cargo test --workspace --lib --features fast-kdf` (297 passed), `cargo clippy -p joy-cli --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nNote: the fix prevents future drift but does not recover entries that were already dropped from a working tree before this commit. To restore them on the affected machine, discard the unstaged `.gitignore` change (so the committed version with all tools is back) and re-run `joy ai init`." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
