2026-05-01T12:08:13.102Z JOY-013F-33 item.created "Switch AI delegations to passphrase-derived keys" [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-01T15:05:02.774Z JOY-013F-33 comment.added "Implementation plan (under this item; closing requires ADR-037 ratification + this work landing):\n\nStep 1 -- Schema (`crates/joy-core/src/model/project.rs`)\n- Add `delegation_salt: Option<String>` to `AiDelegationEntry` with `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]`. Backward-compatible per ADR-035.\n\nStep 2 -- HKDF helper (`crates/joy-core/src/auth/derive.rs`)\n- Add `hkdf` crate to joy-core deps.\n- Add `pub fn derive_delegation_seed(identity_key: &DerivedKey, salt: &Salt, project_id: &str, ai_member_id: &str) -> [u8; 32]`. Uses HKDF-SHA256 with `info = "joy-delegation:" || project_id || ":" || ai_member_id` per ADR-037.\n- Tests: deterministic, per-(salt, project, member) domain separation.\n\nStep 3 -- Bootstrap path (`crates/joy-cli/src/commands/auth.rs::token_add`)\n- Match arm `(None, None)`: generate fresh `delegation_salt`, derive seed via HKDF, save to local cache, write `project.yaml` entry with both `delegation_verifier` and `delegation_salt`.\n- Match arm `(Some, None)` with `delegation_salt` present: derive seed locally from passphrase + salt + info, save to cache, NO `project.yaml` write. New code path -- the multi-machine ergonomic.\n- Match arm `(Some, None)` without `delegation_salt` (legacy entry): keep existing bail with rotate suggestion. Rotation now writes the salt and unblocks future machines.\n- Match arm `(Some, Some)`: unchanged fast path.\n- Match arm `(None, Some)`: unchanged orphan-cache bail.\n\nStep 4 -- Rotate (`crates/joy-cli/src/commands/auth.rs::run_ai_rotate`)\n- Replace random keypair generation with: fresh salt, HKDF-derived seed.\n- Update `delegation_verifier` AND `delegation_salt` AND `rotated:` in a single `project.yaml` write.\n- Save derived seed locally.\n\nStep 5 -- Tests\n- Unit tests for HKDF derivation (deterministic, domain-separated).\n- Bootstrap test: fresh delegation produces salt + verifier consistent with derivation.\n- Multi-machine test: with salt set in yaml and no local cache, derive-and-cache works without yaml write.\n- Rotate test: salt changes, verifier changes, local cache replaced.\n\nStep 6 -- Migration story\n- No automatic migration code in this pass. Existing entries without `delegation_salt` keep working on the machine that has the cached private key (Some, Some) -- the fast path is salt-agnostic. They only show their age when the user tries to use the delegation on a second machine, and the bail message instructs `joy ai rotate`. Rotation under the new code writes the salt and unblocks all future machines.\n- Phase 2 (separate item): explicit `joy ai migrate-delegations` for batch migration.\n\nOut of scope for this pass:\n- `joy ai migrate-delegations` command.\n- Auth.md update.\n\nRollout: implementation lands as a single PR; users on stale binaries continue to work normally (legacy entries verify against legacy verifiers); users on new binaries pick up the multi-machine ergonomic on next rotate or on first use of a project bootstrapped under the new code." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-01T15:05:02.881Z JOY-013F-33 item.status_changed "new -> in-progress" [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-01T15:16:51.432Z JOY-013F-33 comment.added "Implemented in commit 5822c98.\n\nChanges:\n\n- [x] `AiDelegationEntry` (crates/joy-core/src/model/project.rs): added optional `delegation_salt: Option<String>`, gated on `Option::is_none` for backward compat with ADR-033 §1 legacy entries.\n- [x] `derive_delegation_seed` (crates/joy-core/src/auth/derive.rs): HKDF-SHA256 over the human's identity material with `info = "joy-delegation:" || project_id || ":" || ai_member_id`. Uses the `hkdf` crate (added to joy-core deps).\n- [x] `joy auth token add` bootstrap (crates/joy-cli/src/commands/auth.rs): rewritten match expression. (None, None) generates fresh salt and derives. (Some, None) with salt re-derives locally with verifier cross-check, no project.yaml write. (Some, None) without salt bails with rotate suggestion (legacy ADR-033 §1 entry).\n- [x] `joy ai rotate` (crates/joy-cli/src/commands/auth.rs): generates fresh salt, derives seed via HKDF, writes verifier + salt + rotated timestamp in a single project.yaml write. Legacy entries are upgraded on first rotation.\n- [x] Tests: 5 new unit tests in `auth::derive::tests` covering determinism, salt-induced change, project- and member-id domain separation, and identity-key sensitivity. Existing test sites in model/project.rs updated for the new struct field.\n\nVerification:\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib --features fast-kdf`: 302 passed (up from 297; +5 new HKDF tests).\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --features fast-kdf -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo build -p joy-cli`: clean.\n\nOut of scope (Phase 2 follow-up items):\n- `joy ai migrate-delegations` command for explicit batch migration.\n- Auth.md update reflecting the unified passphrase-derivation model.\n- Documentation refresh in CLAUDE.md / ai_templates referencing the new mental model.\n\nSubmitting for review rather than closing -- this is security-critical code and warrants explicit human ratification before being declared done." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
